      "writtenOn": "2026-11-25T12:07:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Suggestion: could you add a test for what keystone requests from Valkey? On `relation_created` as leader, the local app databag should contain `database: \"\u003capp\u003e:*\"` and `requested-secrets`. That `database` value becomes the Valkey ACL key pattern, so it\u0027s the one piece of the contract that\u0027s specific to keystone. Note that in the scenario context the app name defaults to the charm name, so the value is `keystone-k8s:*`, not `keystone:*`. Something like:\n```python\ndef test_requests_acl_key_pattern(self, ctx, complete_state):\n    rel \u003d testing.Relation(endpoint\u003d\"distributed-cache\", remote_app_name\u003d\"valkey\")\n    state_in \u003d dataclasses.replace(\n        complete_state, relations\u003d[*complete_state.relations, rel]\n    )\n    state_out \u003d ctx.run(ctx.on.relation_created(rel), state_in)\n    data \u003d state_out.get_relation(rel.id).local_app_data\n    assert data[\"database\"] \u003d\u003d \"keystone-k8s:*\"\n    assert \"requested-secrets\" in data\n```",
      "revId": "7e0fb2f83796a8e41dd54ff7eaf5346edf61e182",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543"
    },
